    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/manhattanedu/AdjunctFaculty/jobs/5516927/adjunct-faculty-vlsi-chip-design": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, VLSI / Chip Design",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, VLSI / Chip Design Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Manhattan University, Riverdale NY Job Type Faculty Part-Time (Adjunct) Department Electrical & Computer Engineering Opening Date 10/14/2026 Description Benefits Questions About the University: Manhattan University is nestled in the historic neighborhood or Riverdale , close to dozens of restaurants and shops as well as Van Cortlandt Park , and is only 35 minutes from midtown Manhattan. Manhattan University is nationally ranked and offers degree programs in the arts, business, education, engineering, and science. The University has approximately 2,900 full and part-time undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in over 50 fields of study. It is committed to excellence in teaching a diverse student body and preparing students for successful careers and fulfilling lives. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment where all employees and faculty members can thrive personally and professionally. Position Description The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Manhattan University, part of the School of Engineering, focuses on preparing students for careers in electrical engineering, computer engineering, and emerging technology fields. Emphasizing hands-on learning, laboratory experience, faculty mentorship, and practical engineering design, the department invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty member to teach an undergraduate or graduate course in VLSI Design, Digital IC Design, or Chip Design during the Spring 2027 semester. The successful candidate will deliver engaging, hands-on instruction that prepares students for careers and further study in semiconductor technology and integrated-circuit design. This is an in-person, on-campus, non-remote position during the Spring 2027 semester. The instructor must be available to teach the assigned class at the scheduled campus time and participate in required departmental activities. Job Responsibilities Provide high-quality, engaging instruction in an undergraduate or graduate course in VLSI Design, Chip Design, Digital IC Design, or a closely related area. Develop and deliver course materials, including lectures, laboratory activities, assignments, projects, and assessments. Introduce students to modern VLSI and integrated-circuit design methodologies, tools, and industry practices. Incorporate practical examples and applications from semi conduct or technology and chip design. Hold scheduled office hours and provide academic guidance and support to students. Evaluate student assignments, projects, examinations, and laboratory work, providing timely feedback to support student learning. Collaborate with faculty colleagues and participate in departmental meetings and activities as requested by the department chair. Adhere to Manhattan University's mission, values, academic policies, and instructional standards. Requirements Master's degree required in Computer Engineering from an accredited institution. Demonstrated knowledge of VLSI, integrated-circuit design, chip design, or a closely related area. Ability to teach effectively in an in-person classroom environment. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Supplemental Information Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Computer Engineering. Industry experience in semiconductor, ASIC, FPGA, VLSI, SoC, or chip design (optional). Professional experience using industry-standard EDA tools such as Cadence, Synopsys, Siemens EDA, or equivalent platforms. Experience with Verilog/SystemVerilog, RTL design, synthesis, verification, or physical design. Prior college/university teaching experience. Experience supervising hardware design projects, laboratories, or senior design projects. Current professional experience in the semiconductor or technology industry. Preferred Course Expertise: Candidates should be comfortable with some or all of the following topics: CMOS and digital integrated-circuit design. VLSI design methodologies. ASIC and SoC design. Digital logic and RTL design. Verilog/SystemVerilog. Computer-aided VLSI/EDA tools. Logic synthesis and physical design. Timing analysis and verification. FPGA and digital hardware design. Semiconductor fabrication fundamentals. Layout and circuit-level design. Low-power and high-performance IC design. Salary Range Based on Experience: Instructor $1477.28 per credit Assistant Professor $1526.25 per credit Associate Professor $1575.65 per credit Professor $1625.04 per credit Applicants should submit: Current curriculum vitae/resume. Cover letter describing relevant teaching and/or industry experience. Academic transcripts or evidence of degree qualifications. Brief description of VLSI/chip-design expertise. Teaching experience, if applicable. Professional references. Manhattan University is an E-Verify employer. Founded in 1853, Manhattan University is an independent Catholic Lasallian institution located in Riverdale, NY that embraces students of all faiths, cultures, and traditions. The mission of the University is to provide a dynamic student-centered educational experience that prepares graduates for lives of personal development, professional success, civic engagement, and service to their fellow human beings. We expect our faculty, administration, and staff to be knowledgeable about our mission and to make a positive contribution to the mission. Manhattan University provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to age, race, creed, color, sexual orientation, military status, sex, disability, marital status, partnership status, pregnancy, caregiver status, domestic violence victim status, gender identity or expression, arrest or conviction record, criminal history, credit history, national origin, alienage or citizenship status, unemployment status and salary history. Manhattan University values and celebrates diversity and is committed to providing an inclusive environment for all employees. All interested, qualified persons are encouraged to apply. Please note that this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you meet the minimum degree requirements as listed in the posting? Yes No 02 Do you meet the minimum requirements for this position as listed in the posting? Yes No Required Question Employer Manhattan University Address 4513 Manhattan College Pkwy Riverdale, New York, 10471 Apply"
